'''terrane''', ''n.'' See ''terrain.''

'''terranean''' (te-rā′nē-ạn), ''a.'' [< L. ''terra'', earth, + ''-an'' + ''-e-an'' (after ''subterranean'', ''mediterranean'', etc.).] Being in the earth; belonging to the earth, or occurring beneath the surface of the earth.

{{smaller block|The great strain on the trolley wire which would be a necessary incident of ''terranean'' supply renders such a system impracticable.
{{right|''Elect. Rev.'' (Amer.), XVIII. i. 9.}}}}

'''terraneous''' (te-rā′nē-us), ''a.'' [< L. ''terra'', earth, + ''-an'' + ''-e-ous'' (after ''subterraneous'').] In ''bot.'', growing on land.

'''terrapene†''', ''n.'' An obsolete variant of ''terrapin.''

'''Terrapenes''' (ter-a-pē′nēz), ''n. pl.'' [NL.: see ''terrapin.''] A subdivision of ''Emydea'' (which see), in which the pelvis is free, the neck bends in a vertical plane, and the head may be almost completely retracted within the carapace. ''Huxley.'' {{smaller|The group contains such genera as ''Emys'', ''Cistudo'', ''Chelydra'', ''Cinosternum'', and ''Staurotypus''. The other subdivision of ''Emydea'' is ''Chelodines''. See cuts under ''Cinosternum'', ''Cistudo'', and ''terrapin''.}}

